    Make max-attempts of publish-engage take effect (#8320)
    
    The default workflows fast and partial-publish set max-attempts: 2 on
    publish-engage without a retry-strategy. With the default strategy none,
    a failed operation is never retried, so the setting had no effect. Since
    0fc08998e0 (#7890), Opencast logs a warning for this combination, so
    every run of the default workflows warns about its own configuration.
    
    The setting clearly expresses the intent to try publishing twice, and an
    automatic second attempt is reasonable for a publication. Add
    retry-strategy: retry so that max-attempts takes effect as intended. Do
    the same in the operation examples of publish-engage and
    publish-engage-aws in the documentation, which suggest the same
    ineffective combination.
    
    Fixes #8319
    
    > This is the version for 21 which does not modify Opencast's behavior.
    > #8321 fixes this for develop by actually modifying the behavior.
    
